   "assumption": "under the assumption that each hour from the true start of an episode to its recognition multiplies the odds of a bad outcome by 1.02, and that an episode recognised after 6.3 h carries the cited cohort's 27.4% hospital mortality (that anchoring is judgement), which sets the size of every per-100 figure; the 1.02 is the association between the time from a high NEWS to critical care and hospital mortality in one London cohort, an association in other patients, not a measured effect of earlier recognition",
   "difference": {
    "alerts": 973,
    "bins_alerting": 28057,
    "episodes_evaluated": 0,
